_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.02571183955664469,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":50.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12934205264337306,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":89.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.017725129347524213,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":30.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03603898362515445,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":5.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0034894604053064215,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.064050004,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":42.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Plumas Bancorp operates as the bank holding company for the Plumas Bank that provides various banking products and services for small and middle market businesses and individuals. The company accepts various deposits, such as checking, money market checking, business sweep, public funds sweep, savings, and retirement accounts, as well as time and remote deposits. Its loan portfolio comprises personal and commercial loans, real estate, construction, agricultural, and government-guaranteed loans; residential and home equity lines of credit; land development and construction loans; automobile loans; consumer loans; purchased credit deteriorated (PCD) and non-PCD loans; and small business administration loans. In addition, the company provides telephone and mobile banking, internet banking with bill-pay options, cashier's check, bank-by-mail, automated teller machine, night depository, safe deposit box, direct and mobile deposit, electronic funds transfer, FedNow\u00ae-receive Service, and other customary banking services. Plumas Bancorp was founded in 1980 and is headquartered in Reno, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew J. Ryback CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $952,413 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 234 people. Revenue per employee of $420K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $87K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Plumas Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $436M market cap on $98M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 48% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 41-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $20M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.73\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3417366946778723},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Plumas Bancorp (PLBC) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Precision_Trading_with_Plumas_Bancorp_PLBC_Risk_Zones_111326020602_1794553562.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794553562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Plumas Bancorp (NASDAQ:PLBC) and HomeTrust Bancshares (NYSE:HTB)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/comparing-plumas-bancorp-nasdaqplbc-and-hometrust-bancshares-nysehtb.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793755724.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(PLBC) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/PLBC_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110326022202_1793690522.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793690522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Plumas Bancorp (PLBC) to Distribute Quarterly Dividend of $0.33 on November 17th","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/01/plumas-bancorp-plbc-to-distribute-quarterly-dividend-of-0-33-on-november-17th.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793535216.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Plumas Bancorp (PLBC) Q3 Earnings Power Quietly Builds Beneath Calm Stock Reaction","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/plumas-bancorp-plbc-q3-earnings-141510576.html","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792678510.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Plumas Bancorp declares $0.33 dividend (NASDAQ:PLBC)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"ht